IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa12-logic`

-- coa12-ch4a-removal.l4: the Companies Act 2006, Part 16, Chapter 4 "Removal, resignation, etc of auditors", from the heading to s 515:
-- "Removal of auditor" (ss 510, 511, 511A, 512, 513) and "Failure to re-appoint auditor" (ss 514, 515) (lines 7169-7249 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. See coa12-ch3a-report.l4 for how to read an answer. Forks are in NOTES.md.
-- s 512 is blank in this text (repealed). Keel and other-part answers are INPUTS named as PLAN.md 4.1 and 4.2 name them.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 510  Resolution removing auditor from office
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 510(1)
-- Plain gloss: the members may remove an auditor from office at any time.
-- src:7172 | (1) The members of a company may remove an auditor from office at any time.
@ref s 510(1) The members' power to remove an auditor (src:7172-7172)
GIVEN `the persons removing the auditor are members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to be removed is an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 510(1) the members may remove the auditor from office` MEANS
    IF `the persons removing the auditor are members of the company` AND `the person to be removed is an auditor of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The members of a company may remove an auditor from office at any time"

-- COVERS-FORK F7: s 510(2), s 510(2)(a), s 510(2)(b)
-- Plain gloss: the power can be used only by an ordinary resolution at a meeting, after the special notice that s 511 requires. A special resolution also does (s 282(5)).
-- src:7173 | (2) This power is exercisable only—
-- src:7174 | (a) by ordinary resolution at a meeting, and
-- src:7175 | (b) in accordance with section 511 (special notice of resolution to remove auditor).
@ref s 510(2) How the power is exercised (src:7173-7175)
GIVEN `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the resolution was passed at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the removal was in accordance with section 511 (special notice of resolution to remove auditor)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 510(2) the power to remove the auditor has been exercised as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `coa12 both answers hold`
        (`coa12 both answers hold`
            (`coa12 either answer holds` `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution`)
            (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `the resolution was passed at a meeting`))
        (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `the removal was in accordance with section 511 (special notice of resolution to remove auditor)`)
    -- JUST FALSE here is -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This power is exercisable only— (a) by ordinary resolution at a meeting, and (b) in accordance with section 511" (a list closed with "only"; a special resolution counts as an ordinary one by s 282(5): fork F7)

-- COVERS: s 510(3), s 510(3)(a), s 510(3)(b)
-- Plain gloss: removing an auditor does not take away any compensation or damages he is owed for the end of that appointment, or of any appointment that ends with it.
-- src:7176 | (3) Nothing in this section is to be taken as depriving the person removed of compensation or damages payable to him in respect of the termination—
-- src:7177 | (a) of his appointment as auditor, or
-- src:7178 | (b) of any appointment terminating with that as auditor.
@ref s 510(3) Compensation or damages (src:7176-7178)
GIVEN `the compensation or damages are payable to him in respect of the termination of his appointment as auditor or of any appointment terminating with that as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 510(3) the section deprives the person removed of the compensation or damages` MEANS
    IF `the compensation or damages are payable to him in respect of the termination of his appointment as auditor or of any appointment terminating with that as auditor`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section is to be taken as depriving the person removed of compensation or damages payable to him in respect of the termination— (a) of his appointment as auditor, or (b) of any appointment terminating with that as auditor"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of those payments

-- COVERS: s 510(4), s 510(4)(a), s 510(4)(b)
-- Plain gloss: an auditor cannot be removed before his term ends except by this section's resolution or by the court under s 511A. The answer is the BAR: JUST TRUE means the removal is barred.
-- src:7179 | (4) An auditor may not be removed from office before the expiration of his term of office except—
-- src:7180 | (a) by resolution under this section, or
-- src:7181 | (b) in accordance with section 511A.
@ref s 510(4) No removal before the term ends, except (src:7179-7181)
GIVEN `the removal would be before the expiration of his term of office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor is removed by resolution under section 510` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor is removed in accordance with section 511A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 510(4) the auditor is barred from removal before the expiration of his term of office` MEANS
    IF NOT `the removal would be before the expiration of his term of office`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor may not be removed from office before the expiration of his term of office"; the subsection says nothing of removal at or after the end of the term
    ELSE IF `the auditor is removed by resolution under section 510` OR `the auditor is removed in accordance with section 511A`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except— (a) by resolution under this section, or (b) in accordance with section 511A" (an "except" met: fork F6)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 511  Special notice required for resolution removing auditor from office
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 511(1)
-- Plain gloss: a resolution at a general meeting to remove an auditor needs special notice (s 312).
-- src:7183 | (1) Special notice is required for a resolution at a general meeting of a company removing an auditor from office.
@ref s 511(1) Special notice (src:7183-7183)
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution at a general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution removes an auditor from office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511(1) special notice is required for the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is a resolution at a general meeting of the company` AND `the resolution removes an auditor from office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Special notice is required for a resolution at a general meeting of a company removing an auditor from office"

-- COVERS: s 511(2)
-- Plain gloss: when the company receives notice of such a resolution it must immediately send a copy to the auditor it is proposed to remove.
-- src:7184 | (2) On receipt of notice of such an intended resolution the company must immediately send a copy of it to the auditor proposed to be removed.
@ref s 511(2) The company must send a copy to the auditor (src:7184-7184)
GIVEN `the company has received notice of an intended resolution to remove an auditor from office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511(2) the company must immediately send a copy of the notice to the auditor proposed to be removed` MEANS
    IF `the company has received notice of an intended resolution to remove an auditor from office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On receipt of notice of such an intended resolution the company must immediately send a copy of it" (fork F1: a duty whose "on receipt" is unmet; "on" counts as "where", 2026-11-05)

-- The same duty as a deontic rule. "Immediately" is not a number of days, so there is no WITHIN (phrasebook 5.9).
@ref s 511(2) The company must send a copy to the auditor (src:7184-7184)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 511(2) the company's duty to send a copy of the notice to the auditor` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Auditor, "send a copy of the notice of the intended resolution to the auditor proposed to be removed"
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- COVERS: s 511(3)
-- Plain gloss: the auditor may send the company written representations (not unreasonably long) about the resolution and ask that members be told of them.
-- src:7185 | (3) The auditor proposed to be removed may make with respect to the intended resolution representations in writing to the company (not exceeding a reasonable length) and request their notification to members of the company.
@ref s 511(3) The auditor's representations (src:7185-7185)
GIVEN `the person is the auditor proposed to be removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representations are in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representations do not exceed a reasonable length` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511(3) the auditor may make representations and request their notification to members` MEANS
    IF `the person is the auditor proposed to be removed` AND `the representations are in writing` AND `the representations do not exceed a reasonable length`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The auditor proposed to be removed may make ... representations in writing to the company (not exceeding a reasonable length)"

-- COVERS: s 511(4), s 511(4)(a), s 511(4)(b)
-- Plain gloss: unless the representations arrive too late, the company must say in its notice that they were made and send a copy to every member who was sent the notice.
-- src:7186 | (4) The company must (unless the representations are received by it too late for it to do so)—
-- src:7187 | (a) in any notice of the resolution given to members of the company, state the fact of the representations having been made, and
-- src:7188 | (b) send a copy of the representations to every member of the company to whom notice of the meeting is or has been sent.
@ref s 511(4) What the company must do with the representations (src:7186-7188)
GIVEN `the auditor has made representations under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representations are received by the company too late for it to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511(4) the company must state the fact of the representations in its notice and send a copy to every member to whom notice is sent` MEANS
    IF NOT `the auditor has made representations under subsection (3)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection presupposes representations and says nothing where there are none
    ELSE IF `the representations are received by the company too late for it to do so`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must (unless the representations are received by it too late for it to do so)" (fork F6: an "unless" once met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS: s 511(5)
-- Plain gloss: if a copy was not sent out because the representations came too late or because of the company's default, the auditor may require them to be read out at the meeting (and still be heard orally).
-- src:7189 | (5) If a copy of any such representations is not sent out as required because received too late or because of the company's default, the auditor may (without prejudice to his right to be heard orally) require that the representations be read out at the meeting.
@ref s 511(5) The auditor may require the representations to be read out (src:7189-7189)
GIVEN `a copy of the representations is not sent out as required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is because the representations were received too late` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is because of the company's default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511(5) the auditor may require that the representations be read out at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the representations is not sent out as required` AND (`that is because the representations were received too late` OR `that is because of the company's default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a copy of any such representations is not sent out as required because received too late or because of the company's default, the auditor may ... require that the representations be read out at the meeting" (fork F16: a grant named "may" whose plain "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- COVERS: s 511(6)
-- Plain gloss: the copies need not be sent or the representations read out if, on application by the company or anyone else claiming to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied the auditor is using the section to get needless publicity for defamatory matter.
-- src:7190 | (6) Copies of the representations need not be sent out and the representations need not be read at the meeting if, on the application either of the company or of any other person claiming to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the auditor is using the provisions of this section to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter.
@ref s 511(6) Needless publicity for defamatory matter (src:7190-7190)
GIVEN `an application has been made either by the company or by any other person claiming to be aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the auditor is using the provisions of this section to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511(6) copies of the representations need not be sent out and the representations need not be read at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made either by the company or by any other person claiming to be aggrieved` AND `the court is satisfied that the auditor is using the provisions of this section to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Copies of the representations need not be sent out and the representations need not be read at the meeting if, on the application either of the company or of any other person claiming to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the auditor is using the provisions of this section to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter" (the court's judgment is an input, never guessed)

-- COVERS: s 511(6)#L7191
-- Plain gloss: on that application the court may order the company's costs (in Scotland, expenses) to be paid in whole or in part by the auditor, even though he is not a party.
-- src:7191 | The court may order the company's costs (in Scotland, expenses) on the application to be paid in whole or in part by the auditor, notwithstanding that he is not a party to the application.
@ref s 511(6) closing words: costs (src:7191-7191)
GIVEN `the application has been made under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511(6) the court may order the company's costs on the application to be paid in whole or in part by the auditor` MEANS
    IF `the application has been made under subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may order the company's costs ... on the application"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 511A  Public interest companies: application to court to remove auditor from office
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 511A(1)
-- Plain gloss: s 511A applies only to a public interest company (s 519A).
-- src:7193 | (1) This section applies only to a public interest company.
@ref s 511A(1) Applies only to a public interest company (src:7193-7193)
GIVEN `s 519A(1) the company is a public interest company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511A(1) the section applies to the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 519A(1) the company is a public interest company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only to a public interest company."
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the definition of "public interest company" borrows terms of other instruments (s 519A)

-- COVERS: s 511A(2)
-- Plain gloss: the competent authority may apply to the court for an order removing an auditor if it considers there are proper grounds.
-- src:7194 | (2) The competent authority may apply to the court for an order removing an auditor of a company from office if the authority considers that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office.
@ref s 511A(2) The competent authority's application (src:7194-7194)
GIVEN `s 511A(1) the section applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is the competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority considers that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511A(2) the competent authority may apply to the court for an order removing the auditor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 511A(1) the section applies to the company`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only to a public interest company."
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies depends on s 519A
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (NOT `the applicant is the competent authority`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The competent authority may apply"; another applicant is the members' route in subsection (3)
        ELSE IF `the authority considers that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the authority considers that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office" (fork F16: a grant named "may" whose plain "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- COVERS: s 511A(3)
-- Plain gloss: the members may apply to the court for an order removing an auditor if the applicants consider there are proper grounds.
-- src:7195 | (3) The members of a company may apply to the court for an order removing an auditor of the company from office if the applicant or applicants consider that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office.
@ref s 511A(3) The members' application (src:7195-7195)
GIVEN `s 511A(1) the section applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the applicants are members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant or applicants consider that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511A(3) the members may apply to the court for an order removing the auditor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 511A(1) the section applies to the company`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only to a public interest company."
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies depends on s 519A
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (NOT `the applicants are members of the company`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The members of a company may apply"
        ELSE IF `the applicant or applicants consider that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the applicant or applicants consider that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office" (fork F16: a grant named "may" whose plain "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- COVERS: s 511A(6)
-- Plain gloss: a difference of opinion on accounting treatments or audit procedures is not proper grounds.
-- src:7203 | (6) For the purposes of this section, divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures are not to be taken to be proper grounds for removing an auditor from office.
@ref s 511A(6) Divergence of opinions is not proper grounds (src:7203-7203)
GIVEN `the ground is divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511A(6) the ground is taken to be proper grounds for removing the auditor from office` MEANS
    IF `the ground is divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures are not to be taken to be proper grounds for removing an auditor from office"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "proper grounds" is not defined; the court decides

-- COVERS: s 511A(4)
-- Plain gloss: on the authority's application, if the court is satisfied there are proper grounds, it may order the auditor's removal.
-- src:7196 | (4) If the court is satisfied, on hearing an application under subsection (2), that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office, it may make an order removing the auditor from office.
@ref s 511A(4) The court's order on the authority's application (src:7196-7196)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied, on hearing an application under subsection (2), that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground is divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511A(4) the court may make an order removing the auditor on the competent authority's application` MEANS
    IF `the ground is divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures are not to be taken to be proper grounds" (subsection (6))
    ELSE IF `the court is satisfied, on hearing an application under subsection (2), that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is satisfied, on hearing an application under subsection (2), that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office, it may make an order" (fork F16: a grant named "may" whose plain "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- COVERS: s 511A(5), s 511A(5)(a), s 511A(5)(a)(i), s 511A(5)(a)(ii), s 511A(5)(b), s 511A(5)#L7202
-- Plain gloss: on the members' application the court may order removal if the applicants together hold at least 5% of the voting rights of all members who can vote at a general meeting, or at least 5% in nominal value of the share capital, and there are proper grounds.
-- src:7197 | (5) If the court is satisfied, on hearing an application under subsection (3), that—
-- src:7198 | (a) the applicants represent in total—
-- src:7199 | (i) not less than 5% of the voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at a general meeting of the company, or
-- src:7200 | (ii) not less than 5% in nominal value of the company’s share capital, and
-- src:7201 | (b) there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office,
-- src:7202 | the court may make an order removing the auditor from office.
@ref s 511A(5) The court's order on the members' application (src:7197-7202)
GIVEN `the voting rights the applicants represent in total, as a fraction of the voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at a general meeting of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the share capital the applicants represent in total, as a fraction of the company's share capital` IS A NUMBER
      `the court is satisfied that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground is divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 511A(5) the court may make an order removing the auditor on the members' application` MEANS
    IF `the ground is divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures are not to be taken to be proper grounds" (subsection (6))
    ELSE IF       (`the voting rights the applicants represent in total, as a fraction of the voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at a general meeting of the company` AT LEAST 0.05
               OR `the nominal value of the share capital the applicants represent in total, as a fraction of the company's share capital` AT LEAST 0.05)
              AND `the court is satisfied that there are proper grounds for removing the auditor from office`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is satisfied ... that— (a) the applicants represent in total— (i) not less than 5% of the voting rights ..., or (ii) not less than 5% in nominal value of the company's share capital, and (b) there are proper grounds ..., the court may make an order" (fork F16: a grant named "may" whose plain "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 513  Rights of auditor who has been removed from office
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 513(1), s 513(1)(a), s 513(1)(b)
-- Plain gloss: a removed auditor keeps his s 502(2) rights (notices, attending, being heard) for any general meeting at which his term would have expired or at which his place is to be filled.
-- src:7208 | (1) An auditor who has been removed by resolution under section 510 or by order of the court under section 511A has, notwithstanding his removal, the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to any general meeting of the company—
-- src:7209 | (a) at which his term of office would otherwise have expired, or
-- src:7210 | (b) at which it is proposed to fill the vacancy caused by his removal.
@ref s 513(1) The removed auditor's rights (src:7208-7210)
GIVEN `the auditor has been removed by resolution under section 510` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has been removed by order of the court under section 511A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is one at which his term of office would otherwise have expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is one at which it is proposed to fill the vacancy caused by his removal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 513(1) the removed auditor has the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to the meeting` MEANS
    IF (`the auditor has been removed by resolution under section 510` OR `the auditor has been removed by order of the court under section 511A`)
       AND (`the meeting is one at which his term of office would otherwise have expired` OR `the meeting is one at which it is proposed to fill the vacancy caused by his removal`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor who has been removed by resolution under section 510 or by order of the court under section 511A has, notwithstanding his removal, the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to any general meeting of the company— (a) at which his term of office would otherwise have expired, or (b) at which it is proposed to fill the vacancy"

-- COVERS: s 513(2)
-- Plain gloss: in that case "matters concerning the auditor as auditor" in s 502(2) are read as matters concerning him as a former auditor.
-- src:7211 | (2) In such a case the references in that section to matters concerning the auditor as auditor shall be construed as references to matters concerning him as a former auditor.
@ref s 513(2) Matters concerning him as a former auditor (src:7211-7211)
GIVEN `s 513(1) the removed auditor has the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to the meeting` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the auditor attends the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the business of the meeting concerns him as a former auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 513(2) the removed auditor is entitled to be heard on the part of the business` MEANS
    IF `s 513(1) the removed auditor has the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to the meeting` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the auditor attends the meeting` AND `the part of the business of the meeting concerns him as a former auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In such a case the references in that section to matters concerning the auditor as auditor shall be construed as references to matters concerning him as a former auditor"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 514  Failure to re-appoint auditor: special procedure required for written resolution
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 514(2A), s 514(2A)(a), s 514(2A)(b), s 514(2A)(c)
-- Plain gloss: the bar on s 514 applying where the company has no auditor: a period for appointing auditors has ended since the outgoing auditor left; or he left under s 510, 511A or 516; or he has already had the chance to make representations. JUST TRUE means the section is barred from applying.
-- src:7218 | (2A) This section does not apply (by virtue of subsection (2)) if— ”
-- src:7219 | (a) a period for appointing auditors has ended since the outgoing auditor ceased to hold office,
-- src:7220 | (b) the outgoing auditor ceased to hold office by virtue of section 510 , 511A or 516, or
-- src:7221 | (c) the outgoing auditor has previously had the opportunity to make representations with respect to a proposed resolution under subsection (4) of this section or an intended resolution under section 515(4).
@ref s 514(2A) The section does not apply by virtue of subsection (2) if (src:7218-7221)
GIVEN `a period for appointing auditors has ended since the outgoing auditor ceased to hold office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the outgoing auditor ceased to hold office by virtue of section 510, 511A or 516` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the outgoing auditor has previously had the opportunity to make representations with respect to a proposed resolution under section 514(4) or an intended resolution under section 515(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 514(2A) the section is barred from applying by virtue of subsection (2)` MEANS
