-- COVERS: s 515(1), s 515(1)#L7233
-- Plain gloss: at a general meeting of a private company, special notice is required for a resolution that would replace an auditor who is to leave at the end of a period for appointing auditors, unless he leaves under s 510, 511A or 516.
-- src:7232 | (1) Special notice is required for a resolution at a general meeting of a private company whose effect would be to appoint a person as auditor in place of a person (the “outgoing auditor”) who, at the time the notice is given, is an auditor of the company and who is to cease to hold office at the end of a period for appointing auditors.
-- src:7233 | But special notice is not required under this subsection if the auditor is to cease to hold office by virtue of section 510 , 511A or 516.
@ref s 515(1) Private company: a replacement for an outgoing auditor (src:7232-7233)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is a resolution at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution would appoint a person as auditor in place of the outgoing auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the notice is given the outgoing auditor is an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the outgoing auditor is to cease to hold office at the end of a period for appointing auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor is to cease to hold office by virtue of section 510, 511A or 516` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(1) special notice is required for the resolution of a private company` MEANS
    IF       `s 4(1) the company is a private company`
         AND `the resolution is a resolution at a general meeting`
         AND `the resolution would appoint a person as auditor in place of the outgoing auditor`
         AND `at the time the notice is given the outgoing auditor is an auditor of the company`
         AND `the outgoing auditor is to cease to hold office at the end of a period for appointing auditors`
         AND (NOT `the auditor is to cease to hold office by virtue of section 510, 511A or 516`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Special notice is required for a resolution at a general meeting of a private company whose effect would be to appoint a person as auditor in place of a person (the “outgoing auditor”) who, at the time the notice is given, is an auditor of the company and who is to cease to hold office at the end of a period for appointing auditors. But special notice is not required under this subsection if the auditor is to cease to hold office by virtue of section 510 , 511A or 516." (the "where"-like scope and the "if" exception, rulings of 2026-11-05)

