    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection presupposes representations and says nothing where there are none
    ELSE IF `the representations are received by the company too late for it to do so`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must (unless the representations are received by it too late for it to do so)" (fork F6: an "unless" once met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS: s 515(6)
-- Plain gloss: if a copy was not sent out because the representations came too late or because of the company's default, the outgoing auditor may require them to be read out at the meeting.
-- src:7247 | (6) If a copy of any such representations is not sent out as required because received too late or because of the company's default, the outgoing auditor may (without prejudice to his right to be heard orally) require that the representations be read out at the meeting.
@ref s 515(6) The outgoing auditor may require the representations to be read out (src:7247-7247)
GIVEN `a copy of the representations is not sent out as required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is because the representations were received too late` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is because of the company's default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(6) the outgoing auditor may require that the representations be read out at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the representations is not sent out as required` AND (`that is because the representations were received too late` OR `that is because of the company's default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a copy of any such representations is not sent out as required because received too late or because of the company's default, the outgoing auditor may ... require that the representations be read out at the meeting" (fork F16: a grant named "may" whose plain "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- COVERS: s 515(7), s 515(7)#L7249
-- Plain gloss: as s 511(6): needless publicity for defamatory matter; the court may order the outgoing auditor to pay the company's costs.
-- src:7248 | (7) Copies of the representations need not be sent out and the representations need not be read at the meeting if, on the application either of the company or of any other person claiming to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the auditor is using the provisions of this section to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter.
-- src:7249 | The court may order the company's costs (in Scotland, expenses) on the application to be paid in whole or in part by the outgoing auditor, notwithstanding that he is not a party to the application.
@ref s 515(7) Needless publicity for defamatory matter (src:7248-7249)
GIVEN `an application has been made either by the company or by any other person claiming to be aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the auditor is using the provisions of this section to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(7) copies of the representations need not be sent out and the representations need not be read at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made either by the company or by any other person claiming to be aggrieved` AND `the court is satisfied that the auditor is using the provisions of this section to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Copies of the representations need not be sent out and the representations need not be read at the meeting if, on the application either of the company or of any other person claiming to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the auditor is using the provisions of this section to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter"

@ref s 515(7) closing words: costs (src:7249-7249)
GIVEN `the application has been made under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(7) the court may order the company's costs on the application to be paid in whole or in part by the outgoing auditor` MEANS
    IF `the application has been made under subsection (7)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may order the company's costs ... on the application"
